#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this module, you can choose your screen saver, determine how much time "
"must pass before the screen saver is activated, and add or remove password "
"protection to your screen saver."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choosing the screen saver, and configuring its options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Along the left side is a list of all available screen savers. You can select "
"a screen saver by simply clicking on its name. Once you have selected a "
"screen saver, you will see a small preview on the monitor on the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The preview monitor will often show the screen saver larger than it is when "
"the screen saver is activated. This is done on purpose, since many of the "
"details of the screen savers would be unintelligible if actually scaled down "
"to such a small size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each screen saver has a different set of setup options. By clicking on "
"<guilabel>Setup...</guilabel>, a dialog box will appear with all available "
"options. As you adjust the options, the preview box in the dialog box will "
"show you what effect you will achieve with the current settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are done setting up your screen saver, click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> will erase any changes you made in "
"this dialog box, and return you to the screen saver module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking the <guibutton>About</guibutton> button will give you the Copyright "
"and Author information if you are interested."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you think you have all the options set the way you want, simply click "
"on <guibutton>Test</guibutton> to immediately start the screen saver "
"<emphasis>exactly</emphasis> as it will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Settings</guilabel> box is a check box labeled "
"<guilabel>Start automatically</guilabel>. This box must have a mark in it, "
"or &kde; will not launch any screen saver and it will not allow you to "
"adjust the settings of your screen saver."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting the time, priority and passwords for screen savers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the screensaver list is a check box to have the screen saver "
"<guilabel>Start automatically</guilabel>, and a spin box which determines "
"the period of inactivity before the screen saver should be started. You can "
"enter any positive number of minutes in this box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below that is a check box labeled <guilabel>Require password after</"
"guilabel>. If it is checked, when you click a key or click a mouse button to "
"end the screen saver after the time in the spinbox and return to your work, "
"you must enter a password. The password used is the same password you used "
"to login to your machine. If there is no mark in the check box, no password "
"is required to return to your desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a non-&kde; screen saver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; does not prevent another screen saver from working. To use a different "
"screen saver, such as <application>xscreensaver</application>, simply "
"disable the &kde; Screen Saver, and set up your other screen saver program "
"normally."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing and restoring a screen saver from your system"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to remove a screen saver from the list in this &systemsettings; "
"module, you will need to rename a file on your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Working as a <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user is a "
"potentially dangerous situation. While unlikely, it is entirely possible to "
"do permanent damage to your system while working as <emphasis>root</"
"emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "Be very careful following the next set of directions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "To delete a screen saver, type the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>bash$</prompt> <command>cd \n"
"$KDEDIR/kde4/services/ScreenSavers</command>\n"
"<prompt>bash$</prompt> <command>ls</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will give you a list of files. You will notice similarities between "
"some of the file names and that of the screen saver you want to remove. "
"Simply rename the file of similarly named desktop file to a name which does "
"not end in <emphasis>desktop</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>bash$</prompt> <command>cd \n"
"$KDEDIR/share/kde4/services/ScreenSavers</command>\n"
"<prompt>bash$</prompt> <command>mv krandom.desktop krandom.backup</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Will remove Space (GL) from the list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must close the &systemsettings; entirely and restart it before the "
"changes will be seen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To restore the disabled screen saver, simply rename the file back to its "
"original name:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>bash$</prompt> <command>cd \n"
"$KDEDIR/share/kde4/services/ScreenSavers</command>\n"
"<prompt>bash$</prompt> <command>mv krandom.backup krandom.desktop</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restart the &systemsettings;, and the screen saver is back in the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Settings: Grace period"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a five second grace period after the screen saver begins before a "
"password is required even if <guilabel>Require password</guilabel> is "
"checked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Locking the desktop manually, by clicking the lock icon in the &kde; panel, "
"causes the password protection to engage immediately with no grace period."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To alter the grace period setting, you need to manually edit the "
"configuration file. To do so:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>cd <filename>~/.kde/share/config</filename> </"
"command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now, using a text editor (the example uses &kate;, the &kde; text editor), "
"load the <filename>kscreensaverrc</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>kate <filename>kscreensaverrc</filename> </"
"command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Search through the file for an entry entitled <emphasis>LockGrace</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "If the entry exists, you can edit the value of the entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "LockGrace=3000"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The value of the entity represents the duration of the grace period in "
"milliseconds. An entry of 3000, would change the grace period to 3 seconds. "
"You can set the value of the entry to any number between zero (no grace "
"period) and 300000 (5 minutes)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the entry does not exist, simply add the entry to the end of the section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Any changes to the configuration entry take effect immediately."
msgstr ""
